<h1>ARMS — Terms of Service</h1>
<p class="muted">Effective date: 1 November 2026</p>
<h2>The software</h2>
<p>ARMS is open-source software (see the repository license) that runs AI
agents on infrastructure you control. The Gmail connector acts on your mailbox
only through actions you approve: reads run freely; drafts, sends, label
changes, archives, and trashes require your explicit approval in ARMS.</p>
<h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
<p>Keep your OAuth credentials, vault keys, and database passwords secret. Use
a Google account you own. ARMS Gmail with restricted Gmail scopes shows
Google's "unverified app" screen unless the app completes Google's
verification; by continuing you accept that this is self-hosted software you
operate yourself.</p>
<h2>No warranty</h2>
<p>ARMS is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Mail actions you
approve (sends, trashes, label changes) are your actions; review approvals
carefully. To the maximum extent permitted by law, the authors are not liable
for any loss arising from use of the software.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>Material changes to these terms will be posted with a new effective date.
Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>
